cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Bulk RNA-seq Meta-Analysis Pipeline: a reproducible R workflow for
  cross-study differential expression, cell-composition control and
  random-effects meta-analysis
message: >-
  If you use this pipeline in work you are publishing, please cite it using
  these metadata, and cite the underlying methods (DESeq2, apeglm, metafor,
  xCell, sva, limma) as well.
type: software
authors:
  - name: DockVision
    website: "https://github.com/<username>"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<username>/<repository>"
url: "https://github.com/<username>/<repository>"
abstract: >-
  An R pipeline for bulk RNA-seq meta-analysis across published GEO series.
  It fetches and validates each dataset, collapses technical replicates, runs
  differential expression with effect-size shrinkage, quantifies cell-composition
  confounding through marker panels, covariate-adjusted models and xCell
  deconvolution, pools studies with metafor random-effects models reporting
  heterogeneity statistics, and produces a publication-grade figure set. Built
  around the ways cross-study RNA-seq meta-analysis goes wrong rather than around
  the happy path.
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - meta-analysis
  - differential expression
  - bioinformatics
  - DESeq2
  - metafor
  - deconvolution
  - reproducible research
  - GEO
